(1880225, 258022, 47117, '<td valign="top">At first I scored this very low because I thought it was actually a sunset with tree.  Only upon further and deeper study did I notice it is a bonsai tree with base, however, I still can''t see in the photo the actual artificial light source. I can assume it is a bulb, but I prefer to see the actual light source.  Others may have the first assumption I did though, so the subject matter may have been better differently chosen.  I will up my score on this to reflect that it is not an actual sunset with tree.</td>', 'At first I scored this very low because I thought it was actually a sunset with tree.  Only upon further and deeper study did I notice it is a bonsai tree with base, however, I still can''t see in the photo the actual artificial light source. I can assume it is a bulb, but I prefer to see the actual light source.  Others may have the first assumption I did though, so the subject matter may have been better differently chosen.  I will up my score on this to reflect that it is not an actual sunset with tree.', '2005-11-18 14:05:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880228, 257688, 32033, '<td valign="top">I like the shot although to me it looks a bit too much USM</td>', 'I like the shot although to me it looks a bit too much USM', '2005-11-18 14:07:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880232, 256610, 24503, '<td valign="top">Good shot. IMO if the light had been a little more lateral the effect should have been better.</td>', 'Good shot. IMO if the light had been a little more lateral the effect should have been better.', '2005-11-18 14:08:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880234, 257680, 47117, '<td valign="top">The sun and moon are not artificial light sources, not even in shadows and tunnels.  Therefore, to me, this is a free study shot.  Also, I find the edges a bit out of focus as well as the background.  For all of these reasons, I scored you very low on this entry.</td>', 'The sun and moon are not artificial light sources, not even in shadows and tunnels.  Therefore, to me, this is a free study shot.  Also, I find the edges a bit out of focus as well as the background.  For all of these reasons, I scored you very low on this entry.', '2005-11-18 14:08:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880236, 257103, 47117, '<td valign="top">The sunset, sun, or moon, moonlight are not artificial light sources.  I also find this a bit unappealing due to the extreme offset of the silouetted figure.  I had to score this low on both counts.</td>', 'The sunset, sun, or moon, moonlight are not artificial light sources.  I also find this a bit unappealing due to the extreme offset of the silouetted figure.  I had to score this low on both counts.', '2005-11-18 14:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880240, 258172, 47117, '<td valign="top">I don''t see any light source here, much less artificial. I think I can make out one blurry eye?  In that case, I have had to score this shot extremely low for subject matter and focus being lost.</td>', 'I don''t see any light source here, much less artificial. I think I can make out one blurry eye?  In that case, I have had to score this shot extremely low for subject matter and focus being lost.', '2005-11-18 14:10:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880245, 257865, 32033, '<td valign="top">oversharpened IMHO</td>', 'oversharpened IMHO', '2005-11-18 14:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880251, 257136, 32033, '<td valign="top">moon overexposed</td>', 'moon overexposed', '2005-11-18 14:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1880257, 258088, 47117, '<td valign="top">This is the only photo in which I felt deserved a 10 score.  I like it because of the artificial light source chosen, and the fact that you are "working" with that light.  By doing so, you are taking the viewer not only to the source of the artificial light, but to a sense of completion for that light source - using it as intended.  The shot is also very well in focus, and I find it very appealing in b/w.  Nicely done.</td>', 'This is the only photo in which I felt deserved a 10 score.  I like it because of the artificial light source chosen, and the fact that you are "working" with that light.  By doing so, you are taking the viewer not only to the source of the artificial light, but to a sense of completion for that light source - using it as intended.  The shot is also very well in focus, and I find it very appealing in b/w.  Nicely done.', '2005-11-18 14:17:07.000000', NULL, 1),
